# Environment variables example
# Gemini API Key (server-side only, if used)
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Supabase Configuration (Vite client-side public variables)
# Copy this file to .env.local for local development (already git-ignored).
# Find these in Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API:
# - VITE_SUPABASE_URL: Project URL ONLY (e.g. https://your-project-ref.supabase.co) — do NOT append /rest/v1/
# - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Publishable / anon public key ONLY
# NEVER put your Supabase service_role or secret key in a VITE_ variable.
#
# Vercel Deployment:
# Add both VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY under
# Vercel Dashboard -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables before deploying.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
